        ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}^{2}}{7 x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}^{2}}{7 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int u^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{u^{3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{u^{3}}{21}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}^{3}}{21}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
