        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x^{3}}\\cdot 3 x^{2}=\\frac{3}{x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}}{7 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int \\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\int u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}\\cdot \\frac{u^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{u^{2}}{42}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}^{2}}{42}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
